/**
 * The online kit of "IA na contabilidade" (volume 8), as data. The page is
 * pages/BookKit.jsx, at /books/ia-na-contabilidade/kit.
 *
 * Written on 18/10/2026 from the 1.0.0 book: chapters/o-kit.md (the sections
 * the book promises, by name), each chapter's prompt, "O que conferir", "Faça
 * agora", privacy box and "Na reunião da equipe", chapters/introducao.md,
 * chapters/o-que-o-mes-contabil-pede.md (the rule of each date and the
 * scoreboard) and chapters/dez-coisas-que-nunca-se-cola.md; the kit texts of
 * research/para-o-kit.md; and KDP.md (what the store description promises).
 * The links are the URLs of the series bibliography (books/research/
 * referencias.yaml) for the keys the book cites, with the date they were read.
 *
 * The training material, the follow-ups and the first-pass answers were copied
 * by script, without retyping, from the test transcripts (research/testes/
 * t*.txt, the conversation of each chapter prompt and of each first-pass
 * answer named in research/para-o-kit.md); the scoreboard, word for word from
 * the opening chapter; the ten things, from the closing chapter. A script
 * checked each prompt against the chapter that prints it (18/10/2026: 28 of
 * 28 identical). Whoever edits a prompt here checks it against the chapter.
 *
 * Every prompt in TASKS is the one printed in the chapter, word for word,
 * print line breaks joined, with the material in {fields}; each field's
 * placeholder is the chapter's bracket, so a field left empty prints the
 * chapter's text. The prompt with the training material pasted, as it ran, is
 * the `material` of the chapter's exercise. The follow-ups (the second message
 * of each test conversation) are text templates, as they ran. Words the AI
 * must write ("conferir", "revisar", "não está aqui", "não está na lista",
 * "não está no contrato", "prática do escritório") stay as they are. The date,
 * the month and the kind of client written in a prompt are the test's; the
 * reader changes them, and the hint says so.
 *
 * The first-pass answers ("a versão sem IA") are whole, as they came, with the
 * markup, without the emoji (BookKit shows no emoji). In chapter 12 the
 * invented names, CPF, CNPJ, phone and links of the first-pass material are
 * codes ([Cliente A] to [Cliente F], [CPF], [CNPJ], [telefone], [link
 * retirado]), as the chapter prompt has them; the rest is the AI's text.
 *
 * Dates as the book has them: the rules read on 09/10/2026, the review's lines
 * on 13/10/2026, the MEI lines on 04/10/2026 (volume 5 copies). What was read
 * in Internet Archive copies of gov.br pages during the electoral period, and
 * what KDP.md lists to reopen (the malha letters, the national NFS-e, the
 * cancelling of the option, the year's tables), says "a reconferir": it is
 * reopened live after 26/10/2026 and changes here, with the date. The
 * addresses of the services where the client checks a letter or a guide
 * (e-CAC, Meu Imposto de Renda, Portal do Simples, DTE-SN) are "em releitura"
 * until then, without the address (research/para-o-kit.md, Cap. 12).
 *
 * The 25 transcript files (o-kit.md, "Os testes", "inteiras, como vieram")
 * are not in the page's data, which they would make too heavy: they are
 * served as files, public/books/ia-na-contabilidade/testes/<file>.txt, and
 * the "Os testes" band links each one (TRANSCRIPTS). Copied on 19/10/2026
 * by script from research/testes/t*.txt, all 25 that the analyses
 * (ANALISE-t01-t07.md, ANALISE-t08-t14.md) count, with a 3-line header (the
 * book, the test, the date of the run) and nothing else changed but what
 * privacy takes out, marked "[retirado]": the e-mail addresses that are not
 * on a reserved domain (in t12 and t12b). The Receita's CNPJ for the DAS Pix
 * is the official one, the subject of t12, and stays. Whoever copies them
 * again runs the same checks: e-mail, the account's name, CPF and CNPJ with
 * a valid check digit, real phone numbers, local paths.
 */

